@@ -9,6 +9,21 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## Local resources
+
+Open **Local resources** in the header (at `/devtools-times/local-network`),
+select the local network or this computer, enter the service's HTTP/HTTPS URL,
+and click **Connect**. Requests run in the user's browser, so loopback refers
+to their computer, not the application server. No connection runs on page load.
+
+Deploy the application over HTTPS. The browser may ask for Local network or
+Loopback network permission; blocked access can be restored in site settings.
+The service must return standard CORS headers allowing the application's origin
+(`Access-Control-Allow-Origin`); requests omit credentials. The app declares
+`targetAddressSpace` to support HTTP local services in browsers that implement
+Local Network Access. Other browsers fall back to normal fetch behavior and may
+require HTTPS on the target service. Responses are displayed as text.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
